                <div class="title">Protocol Handling</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="page-content">
            <div class="block block-strong inset text-align-center">
                <twig:ux:icon
                    name="material-symbols:language"
                    class="icon color-primary"
                    width="80"
                    height="80"
                    alt="Protocol Handling"
                />
                <h1>Protocol Handling</h1>
                <p>Protocol handling enables web apps to register their ability to open links with particular URL schemes.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="block block-strong inset">
                <p class="no-margin">
                    A registered protocol associates a custom URL scheme with an app. When a <code>web+symphone</code> link is opened and Symphone is selected as its handler, the operating system can launch the installed app and pass the link to it.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2 class="block-title block-title-medium">Before you test</h2>
            <div class="block block-strong inset">
                <p class="no-margin-top">
                    Install Symphone first so your browser and operating system can register it as a handler for <code>web+symphone</code> links.
                </p>
                <a href="{{ path('app_feature_installation') }}" class="button button-tonal button-large">
                    Check installation
                </a>
                <p class="text-color-gray no-margin-bottom">
                    A regular browser tab cannot reliably determine whether the same PWA is already installed elsewhere on the device. The Installation demo reports the states the browser makes available.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2 class="block-title block-title-medium">Test the protocol handler</h2>
            <div class="block block-strong inset">
                <p class="no-margin-top">
                    Protocol handling is best tested from a browser context outside the installed app. The direct link opens in a new context so the browser or operating system can offer Symphone as its handler.
                </p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 medium-grid-cols-2 grid-gap">
                    <a
                        href="web+symphone://open"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                        class="external button button-fill button-large"
                    >
                        Open with Symphone
                    </a>
                    <button type="button" class="button button-tonal button-large" @click="${copyProtocolLink}">
                        Copy protocol link
                    </button>
                </div>

                <ol>
                    <li>Choose “Open with Symphone”.</li>
                    <li>Approve the browser or operating-system prompt if one appears.</li>
                    <li>Symphone should open at its locale-neutral homepage.</li>
                </ol>

                <p class="text-color-gray no-margin-bottom">
                    If the button does not show a prompt, copy the protocol link, close or minimize Symphone, and paste it into the address bar of a supported browser.
                </p>

            </div>

            <h2 class="block-title">How it is registered</h2>
            <div class="block block-strong inset">
                <p>
                    PWA Bundle adds <code>web+symphone</code> to the manifest’s <code>protocol_handlers</code> member. Its <code>%s</code> placeholder receives the encoded protocol URL. Symphone’s handler route validates that URL before redirecting to the locale-neutral homepage.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="block-footer margin-bottom">
                Protocol handling requires browser and operating-system support and may require Symphone to be installed. The platform controls the confirmation and app-selection experience.
